
-->DBMS stores data in tables with rows and columns.
-->DBMS is used when structure is fixed and relations are important.
Ex : orders

-->MongoDB stores data in JSON-like documents.
-->Data structure is not fixed and can change easily.
-->MongoDB is used when data is large, schema changes frequently, and the application needs high scalability and performance

-->For Sql structure is fixed mongo db is not fixed 
-->We chose MongoDB for nested configurations like data inside data. MongoDB allows us to store single document, which avoids complex joins and makes read operations faster.
--> Campaigns are primarily read-heavy, retrieved as a whole for execution and analytics, and MongoDB fits that access pattern well.
For entities with strict relationships and transactional consistency—like users, billing, and permissions—we still use SQL. So the choice was data-driven, not technology-driven.

